    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Progress Bar\r\n\r\n**Goal**: Use a **for loop** to make the bar fill from 0% to 100% in 10% increments. Each step appears one after another with a short pause.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Do This\r\n\r\n1. **Find where to write your loop** inside the `fillBar()` function.\r\n\r\n2. Use a **for loop** that starts at 10 and ends at 100, counting by 10.\r\n   \r\n3. Inside your loop, use the loop variable to change the bar's width. \r\n\t\r\n    **Syntax:**\r\n\r\n   ```js\r\n   bar.style.width = \"50%\";\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n4. Use `setTimeout()` to delay each step so the fill happens over time.\r\n\r\n   * Hint: multiply your delay by the **loop variable** to stagger the timing.\r\n\r\n5. Make sure to **reset the bar** to `\"0%\"` before running your loop again.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary>Need help? Ask the AI Tutor.</summary>\r\n  \t<ol>\r\n      \t<li>\"How can I use a for loop to fill the bar in 10% steps?\"</li>\r\n  \t\t<li>\"How does setTimeout make the bar move gradually?\"</li>\r\n  \t\t<li>\"What does the loop variable control here?\"</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n\r\n</details>",
